The comment `@@@ The cloned collection has one more element than the original collection.` is incorrect, as cloning a collection should result in a copy with the same number of elements, not one more. However, we are asked to write an assert statement corresponding to the comment as if it were a specification.

Given that the comment states the cloned collection has one more element than the original, we compare the size of the cloned collection (`\result`) with the original (`\old(this.size())`).

Since the method returns the clone, we use `\result` to refer to the cloned set.

<code>assert ((HashSet)\result).size() == \old(this.size()) + 1;</code>
